==English==

===Etymology===
From {{ME.}} {{term|iniquite|lang=enm}}, from {{L.}} {{term|iniquitas|lang=la}}, from {{term|iniquus|lang=la||unjust, harmful}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|iniquities}}

# [[deviation|Deviation]] from right, [[wickedness]], [[gross]] [[injustice]].
#: {{rfdate}} ''The path of righteousness is beset on all sides by the '''iniquities''' of evil men'' — [[w:Ezekiel 25:17|Ezekiel 25:17]]
# A [[wrongful]] [[act]].
# [[absence|Absence]] of [[moral]] or [[spiritual]] [[values]], [[lawlessness]].
# [[denial|Denial]] of the [[sovereignty]] of [[God]].

